{start_of_verse}
The [A]body's a temple and [D]that's what we're taught
Well, [E]I treated this one like an [D]old honky [A]tonk
Greasy cheeseburgers and [D]cheap cigarettes
[E]One day they'll get me if they [D]ain't got me [A]yet
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I'm [A]living in [G]fast [D]forward
[E]Hillbilly rock star [D]out of cont[A]rol
I've been living in [G]fast [D]forward
Now I [E]need to rewind real [A]slow
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
My [A]friends all grew up and [D]they settled down
Built [E]nice little houses on the [D]outskirts of [A]town
They work in their office and [D]drive SUVs
They [E]pray for their babies and they [D]worry about [A]me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge}
[D]I'm always runnin'
[A]Son-of-a-gunnin'
[E]I've had a good time it's [A]true
But the [D]way I've been going
It's [A]time that I tone it [B7]down just a notch or [E]two
{end_of_bridge}

